    "searchText": "Advanced Reporting and Performance Term 2 2026 summative assessment \n1 \n \nSECTION 1 (39 marks) \nRodrique \nYou are the financial controller of Rodrique Ltd (Rodrique) and have responsibility for the \npreparation of Rodrique’s financial statements for the year ended 31 January 2026. \nRodrique is an unquoted, medium-sized company and prepares its financial statements \nin accordance with IFRS Accounting Standards. \nThe main business activity of Rodrique is the manufacture of customised industrial \nfurnaces. You need to advise on, and account for, any revenue arising on the contract \ndescribed in Appendix 1. \nRodrique carries out research and development on new and improved furnaces. Your \nassistant has accounted for research and development costs incurred in the year ended \n31 January 2026.  Relevant information is in Appendix 2. \nRodrique obtained a new bank loan during the year ended 31 January 2026. Information \nabout the bank loan is in Appendix 3. \nYou need to construct the statement of profit or loss of Rodrique for the year ended 31 \nJanuary 2026. The draft statement is in Appendix 4. \nThe remuneration relating to the research director of Rodrique, who was appointed in \nFebruary 2025, has been omitted from the directors’ remuneration disclosure in error.  You \nhave been asked to advise on what amounts should be included in the remuneration \ndisclosure. Relevant information is in Appendix 5. \nQUESTIONS: \nQuestion 1 \nAdvise, using the information in Appendix 1, on the recognition and measurement of \nrevenue arising on the contract for the year ended 31 January 2026 and prepare, showing \nall workings, any journal entries necessary. \n(12 marks) \nQuestion 2 \nAdvise, using the information in Appendix 2, on how the research and development costs \nincurred in the year ended 31 January 2026 should be accounted for and prepare, showing \nall workings, any journal entries necessary. \n(10 marks) \nQuestion 3 \nAdvise, using the information in Appendix 3, on how the bank loan should be accounted \nfor in the year ended 31 January 2026 and prepare, showing all workings, any journal \nentries necessary. \n(9 marks) \n \n \n Advanced Reporting and Performance Term 2 2026 summative assessment \n2 \n \nQuestion 4 \nConstruct the statement of profit or loss of Rodrique for the year ended 31 January 2026 \nusing the information in Appendix 4 and taking account of any adjustments from Questions \n1, 2 and 3. \nYou must complete this question using the Excel spreadsheet provided. \n(4 marks) \nQuestion 5 \nAdvise, using the information in Appendix 5, which amounts should be included in the \ndirectors’ remuneration disclosure note for the year ended 31 January 2026 in relation to \nthe research director. \n(4 marks) \n(Total: 39 marks) \nNotes: \nAll journal entries should be in £’000. \nIgnore the tax effect of any adjustments. \n \n \n \n Advanced Reporting and Performance Term 2 2026 summative assessment \n3 \n \nAPPENDIX 1 (Section 1) \nContract with Fermina \n• \nIn April 2025 Rodrique and its customer Fermina entered into a contract under which \nRodrique would supply and install an industrial furnace for Fermina. The contract \nalso requires Rodrique to reline the furnace five years after installation, a common \nmaintenance requirement for furnaces.  \n• \nThe total contract price was £890,000 of which Fermina paid £50,000 as a deposit \non agreement of the contract.  \n• \nYou are satisfied that the contract meets the definition of a contract for revenue under \nIFRS 15 Revenue from Contracts with Customers. \n• \nThe furnace was delivered to Fermina in August 2025, and installation was \ncompleted by the end of September 2025 when Fermina formally accepted the \nfurnace and paid the remaining balance of £840,000. \n• \nAs the furnace was unique there was not an observable stand-alone selling price for \nthe furnace or the relining. \n• \nRodrique estimates stand-alone selling prices using the cost plus a margin approach. \n• \nThe furnace cost £590,000 to manufacture and install and is expected to result in a \nprofit margin of £177,000 when sold. It is estimated that the relining will cost \n£120,000, and will be sold for £168,000, including a profit margin of £48,000.  \n• \nThe only accounting entries for the contract to date have been to record the £50,000 \ndeposit received as a contract liability and the £840,000 received as revenue. \n  \n \n \n Advanced Reporting and Performance Term 2 2026 summative assessment \n4 \n \nAPPENDIX 2 (Section 1) \nInformation about research and development costs \n• \nOn 1 April 2025 Rodrique started a project to develop a more energy-efficient burner \nfor use in furnaces.  \n• \nThe project met all the criteria in IAS 38 Intangible Assets for the recognition of an \nintangible asset on 1 July 2025. Development and testing were completed by 30 \nNovember 2025 and production of the more energy-efficient burners commenced on \n1 December 2025. \n• \nIt is estimated that the new burners will be used in furnaces for six years. \n• \nYour assistant has recognised the following costs relating to the burner project as an \nintangible asset: \n \nNote \n£’000 \nStaff costs \n1 \n640 \nDepreciation  \n2 \n112 \nAdvertising new burner \n \n128 \nTesting prototype \n3 \n62 \n \n \n942 \nNote: \n1. \nThese are the costs of staff working on the project from 1 April 2025 to 30 \nNovember 2025 which were incurred evenly over that period. \n2. \nThis is depreciation of equipment used on the project from 1 July to 30 \nNovember 2025. \n3. \nCosts relate to the final testing of prototype burners in November 2025. \n• \nNo other accounting entries have been made regarding the project. \n• \nResearch and development costs recognised as an expense, including amortisation, \nis presented in cost of sales. \n \nAPPENDIX 3 (Section 1) \nInformation about bank loan \n• \nRodrique obtained a £4,000,000 5-year bank loan on 1 August 2025. Rodrique \nreceived £3,960,000 on that date as the bank deducted £40,000 as an arrangement \nfee. Your assistant recorded a liability of £3,960,000. \n• \nThe bank loan carries interest of 3.5% per six months and interest is payable on 31 \nJanuary and 31 July each year. Interest paid on 31 January 2026 has been \npresented in general and administrative expenses in profit or loss. The effective rate \nof interest is 3.6% per six months. \n• \nNo other accounting entries have been made regarding the loan. \n \n Advanced Reporting and Performance Term 2 2026 summative assessment \n5 \n \nAPPENDIX 4 (Section 1) \nDraft statement of profit or loss of Rodrique for the year ended 31 January 2026 \nDraft \n£'000 \nRevenue \n14,640 \nCost of sales \n(8,320) \nGross profit \n6,320 \nOther operating income \n23 \nSelling expenses \n(470) \nGeneral and administrative expenses \n(748) \nOperating profit \n5,125 \nProfit before financing and income taxes \n5,125 \nInterest expenses on borrowings \n(335) \nProfit before income taxes \n4,790 \nIncome tax expense \n(872) \nPROFIT \n3,918 \n \nAlso provided as an Excel resource \n \nAPPENDIX 5 (Section 1) \nInformation regarding research director \nThe following information has been obtained regarding the research director for the year \nended 31 January 2026: \n \n£ \nGross salary \n105,000 \nEmployee’s pension contribution \n18,000 \nValue of share options granted \n22,000 \nEmployer’s national insurance contribution  \n10,625 \n  \nEND OF SECTION \n \n \n \n",
